    "body": "## Motivation\n\nQwen3.8-27B (and other dense Qwen3.5-architecture hybrids) use 48 v-heads over 16 k-heads in their GDN layers, a v/k head ratio of 3. #34859 taught `fused_qkvzba_split_reshape_cat_contiguous` to handle non-power-of-two groups through a per-head walk, and enabled ratio 3 on CUDA. The AITER tuple in `qwen3_5.py` was left at `(1, 2, 4, 8)`. On ROCm, every GDN layer of these models therefore still takes the unfused fallback on every forward pass: `torch.split`, two `.contiguous()` copies, and a `torch.cat`.\n\nThe kernel itself has no CUDA-specific code on this path, and the existing ratio-3 unit test is already registered for AMD CI.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/srt/models/qwen3_5.py`: add `3` to `_GDN_FUSED_QKVZBA_RATIOS` when `_use_aiter` is set (`(1, 2, 4, 8)` -> `(1, 2, 3, 4, 8)`), and update the comment. CUDA, CPU and non-AITER HIP are unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe fused kernel is pure data movement. `test/registered/attention/test_gdn_fused_split_head_ratios.py` checks it bit-exactly against plain slicing for ratios 1, 2, 3 and 4. On MI355X (ROCm 7.x, torch 2.11.0+rocm, `SGLANG_USE_AITER=1`), with this branch's source:\n\n```\ntest_ratio_1 PASSED\ntest_ratio_2 PASSED\ntest_ratio_3 PASSED\ntest_ratio_4 PASSED\n4 passed in 4.12s\n```\n\nIn the same environment, `sglang.srt.models.qwen3_5._GDN_FUSED_QKVZBA_RATIOS` resolves to `(1, 2, 3, 4, 8)`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThis change removes two copies and a concat per GDN layer per forward pass on ROCm for ratio-3 models. That is the same path CUDA already takes for this layout. I have not run an end-to-end benchmark for this one-line routing change.\n\nRelated: #31091 generalizes the ratio whitelist for every backend. #43366 (draft) skips the split entirely for batched Triton decode by using strided views. This PR is the minimal fix, so that the ROCm prefill/extend path, and decode outside #43366, matches CUDA.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (existing ratio-3 test, already registered for AMD CI)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (n/a)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37935889607](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37935889607)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37935889207](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37935889207)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37935889423](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37935889423)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
